=== PE 894: Spiral of Theodorus ===

The Spiral of Theodorus is constructed from right triangles
with legs (1, √k) giving hypotenuse √(k+1).

=== Geometric properties ===
  k-th triangle: legs = 1 and √k, hyp = √(k+1)
  Rotation angle: arctan(1/√k) ≈ 1/√k for large k
  Total angle after N: ≈ 2√N
  Distance from origin after N: √(N+1)

=== Asymptotic spiral equation (r, φ) ===
  φ ≈ 2√(r² - 1) → r ≈ φ²/4 + 1
  This is approximately an Archimedean spiral.

=== Interesting values ===
  φ_16 ≈ 2π (first full rotation near 16 triangles)
  φ_300 ≈ 10π (about 5 full rotations)
  The spiral never closes (irrational rotations).

PE answer: 0.7718678168
